.TH SURFACECHECK 1 "2026-08-31" "SurfaceCheck 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
surfacecheck \- local, evidence-backed Omarchy surface inspection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B surfacecheck
.I command
.B --json
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every invocation requires exactly one
.B --json
flag and emits one bounded schemaVersion 1 JSON envelope. Captures are owned
by the optional local
.B surfacecheckd
user service. A missing compositor, tool, adapter, or service is reported as
an explicit status; it is never represented as an empty successful capture.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Report daemon, capture-tool, agent, handoff, and quota state.
.TP
.B service
Query the authenticated local service directly.
.TP
.B capture window | capture region
Capture the active window or launch the bounded region selector.
.TP
.B capture application ADDRESS
Capture the exact Hyprland hexadecimal window address.
.TP
.B review CAPTURE_ID
Run deterministic review. Add
.B --agent --consent-local
for an explicit local agent review.
.TP
.B compare BEFORE_ID AFTER_ID
Compute before/after pixel and perceptual metrics.
.TP
.B select-before-after SESSION BEFORE_ID AFTER_ID
Persist the comparison relationship in the local manifest.
.TP
.B annotate SESSION --note NOTE
Replace the local user note.
.TP
.B export SESSION
Write a deterministic local USTAR evidence archive.
.TP
.B handoff premonition FINDING_ID --consent-external
Request an explicitly consented versioned Premonition handoff.
.TP
.B cancel OPERATION_ID GENERATION
Cancel only the matching active operation generation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --session SESSION
Use a bounded opaque session identifier.
.TP
.B --note NOTE
Attach a bounded plain-text note to a capture or annotation.
.TP
.B --alias ALIAS
Supply an optional already-redacted application label.
.TP
.B --json
Required exactly once.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means the operation succeeded. 1 is an internal or tool error, 2 is an
invalid request or evidence, 3 means the service or adapter is unavailable, 4
means a required capture tool is missing, 5 means the user cancelled, 6 means
another operation is busy, and 7 means the bounded operation timed out.  The
JSON envelope remains the authoritative detailed status.
.SH FILES
The service socket is beneath
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/surfacecheck/
and evidence is beneath the private XDG state directory. Responses expose
only opaque relative export paths.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR surfacecheckd (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
